{
  "id": "redirects-glob-source",
  "description": "Glob `*` source crosses path segments — reference's `sourceMatches` at serve-handler/src/index.js:38-67 pre-substitutes `*` with `(.*)` then calls `pathToRegExp`, so `/dir/*` matches both `/dir/page` (one segment) and `/dir/sub/page` (multi segment). Locks the redirect-side of this behavior so a future regression on the `*`-source routing classifier shows up in the oracle. Closes Codex round 1 P1 and round 2 P1: JS `String.prototype.replace('*', '(.*)')` replaces only the FIRST `*` — so a source like `/a/*/b/*` does NOT over-match (the trailing `*` becomes a path-to-regexp kleene modifier that doesn't fire on multi-segment trailing paths). Also covers `**`-collapse: `/dir/**` matches like `/dir/*`.",
  "fixture": {
    "files": {
      "_marker.txt": "marker\n"
    },
    "serveJson": {
      "redirects": [
        { "source": "/dir/*", "destination": "/elsewhere" },
        { "source": "/face/**", "destination": "/double-star-hit" },
        { "source": "/a/*/b/*", "destination": "/multi-hit" },
        { "source": "/dot/.*/b/*", "destination": "/dot-hit" },
        { "source": "/bracket/*/b/[.]y", "destination": "/bracket-hit" },
        { "source": "/gs/**/b/*", "destination": "/gs-hit" }
      ]
    }
  },
  "runner": {
